The 40-hour figure may come from a different source. The UAE federal government adopted a shorter week (a 4.5-day week with Friday half-days) in 2022, and that applies to federal government staff. Some private employers also choose shorter weeks. Neither changes the statutory maximum for private-sector employees in the Decree-Law, and I couldn't check this against the current text of the law.

