I'm confident in 0.5. Article 84 of the Saudi Labor Law (Royal Decree No. M/51) sets the end-of-service award at half a month's wage for each of the first five years. It sets a full month's wage for each year after the fifth. The figure of 1 is probably the rate for years beyond five, not for the first five.

The question asks for the "full" award, and that could be read as meaning the full-month rate. But the wording is about each of the first five years, and for that period the law gives 0.5 months. Article 85 reduces the award to a third or two-thirds when the employee resigns before completing five or ten years of service. That doesn't change the 0.5 rate for the first five years.

