I'm keeping 12 months. Article L1471-1, paragraph 2 of the Code du travail (introduced by the 2017 Macron ordinances) says any action concerning the termination of an employment contract is time-barred 12 months after the termination is notified.

The figure of 24 months is probably a mix-up with the former rule, which gave 2 years for actions on the performance or termination of the contract. That rule applied before the 2013 and 2017 reforms. The 2013 reform created a 2-year period for actions on performance of the contract, which is still in L1471-1 paragraph 1. A 2-year period also applies to actions for economic dismissal under L1235-7, which was reduced to 12 months in 2017.

